Humans wear clothes (any four reasons):

1. to **keep warm** in cold weather: clothes trap a layer of air and insulate the body;
2. to **protect the skin from the sun** (strong heat and ultraviolet rays) and from the rain;
3. to **protect the body from injuries**, thorns, insect bites and dirt;
4. for **decency** (modesty);
5. for **culture, religion and fashion**, to show identity or job (uniforms) and to look attractive;
6. for special protection at work (overalls, gloves, helmets).
